UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Two of Wands represents the absolute archetype of "Strategic Expansion"—the critical phase where the initial, impulsive fire of the Ace is brought under the control of the analytical, forecasting mind. This is the moment of the "architectural survey," where the sovereign consciousness stands atop the battlements of its own established reality, holding the globe of its potential in one hand while surveying the horizon for the next necessary vector of growth. Moving beyond the pure, raw initiation of the Ace, the Two of Wands signifies a transition from blind, kinetic force to disciplined, long-range planning. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "probabilistic navigation," where you are no longer merely acting on impulse but are actively constructing a framework to support your long-term creative trajectory. Visually, the figure is often depicted looking out from a castle, representing the security you have already earned, while the second wand—held or placed firmly—represents the new, untested territory you are currently scoping out. When the Two of Wands appears, your system is registering a "high-level strategic alignment" status; you are being invited to move beyond your current operational boundaries and to conceive of a future that exists outside of your immediate, day-to-day conditions. This is the archetype of the "Visionary Commander," someone who understands that the primary difference between a fantasy and a manifest reality is the presence of a coherent, well-researched strategy. It commands you to step out of the comfort zone of your existing mastery, to identify the precise points on your horizon where your energy can be most effectively deployed, and to initiate the necessary, ego-stripping work of detachment—you must be willing to leave behind the safety of the current "castle" if you are to truly inhabit the vast, undiscovered territories of your own potential. To inhabit the Two of Wands is to master the art of "controlled projection," understanding that your focus is a high-precision instrument and that by deliberately placing your intention on a specific target, you are already collapsing the distance between where you are and where you intend to be. It is the cosmic affirmation that you possess both the history to ground your plans and the foresight to transcend them, leaving you perfectly poised to initiate the expansion that will define the next cycle of your sovereign existence.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Two of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "strategic myopia," "territorial fragmentation," or the systemic failure to connect your foundational power with your future-oriented objectives. The reversal suggests that you have allowed your perspective to become trapped within the narrow, low-vibration confines of your current, ego-constructed reality, losing sight of the expansive horizon that you are inherently capable of navigating. You are essentially "trapped in the castle," running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that prioritizes the preservation of your past achievements over the risk of future growth, leading to a profound, chronic state of stagnation, intellectual restlessness, and the suffocating feeling of being "ready for more" but having no idea how to safely initiate the departure. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of hesitation"; you are obsessed with the maintenance of your current position, terrified that even the smallest step toward expansion will jeopardize the stability you have worked so hard to achieve, which leads to a profound, systemic misalignment where your actions are perpetually disconnected from your actual, long-term vision. The reversed Two of Wands exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of moving into the "unknown" where your status, your expertise, and your current self-definitions might not hold the same weight or provide the same comfort. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these fear-based, conservative scripts, perform a brutal audit of your current "castle" walls, and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to look toward the horizon. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance insulation, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, expansive agency. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of breaking the deadlock—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the safety of your current status over the potential of your future, and realizing that until you are willing to look beyond your present limits, you will continue to be starved by the very stability you have worked so hard to manifest.'
WHERE id = 16;
